    "text": "WCAX\nwebsite\nAlburg\nThe natural wonders of Alburgh\nBy Darren Perron,7 hours ago\nALBURGH, Vt. (WCAX) - Alburgh is the most northwesterly town in Vermont, a peninsula extending from the border of Canada into Lake Champlain. The community was chartered in 1781, and its population is just over 2,100. As part of our new Wednesday series “Vermont’s Own,” where we’re visiting every town and city across the state in the coming years, Darren Perron gets the dirt on Alburgh.\n1\nComments\nLoading editor...",
